
Simplroutine


The software application I would like to create is a scheduling and productivity app designed for everyday people and students. The main purpose of the application is to help users organize their schedules, manage responsibilities, set goals, and stay productive all in one convenient location. Instead of requiring users to switch between multiple applications for their calendar, tasks, goals, and notes, this application combines these core productivity functions into one cohesive, easy-to-use platform.


Functionality & Features  

Flexible Calendar System & Custom Event Details: Users can view their schedules through monthly, weekly, daily, and yearly views. The monthly calendar provides a big-picture view of major events, appointments, and deadlines, while the daily view includes hourly time-blocking for detailed planning. Users can set recurring tasks and events on specific days of the week (e.g., classes running every Monday and Wednesday). Clicking on any scheduled task or appointment opens an inline notes section where users can add specific details, reminders, or agendas directly associated with that entry.

Dedicated Homework & Academic Tracker: Designed specifically with students in mind, a dedicated homework section allows users to input their courses and manage individual assignments. Each assignment can be customized with a due date, specific submission time, urgency indicator (high/medium/low priority), course tag, and additional project notes.

Goal Setting & Task Management: Users can create short-term and long-term goals, breaking them down into actionable steps. Progress bars, monthly intentions, and motivational reminders help keep users on track. The task management module allows users to filter and sort general to-do items by priority, category, or status.

Usability & Personalization: A built-in notes module captures general thoughts, lists, and reference materials. Users can personalize their planner with custom categories, color-coded tags, and configurable reminders for upcoming deadlines.


Framework, UI & Technology Stack Architecture

To ensure the application is accessible across both desktop computers and mobile devices with appropriate view constraints, the software will be built using a modern full-stack web architecture containerized with Docker:

Frontend UI (React.js + Tailwind CSS): The user interface will be built using React, providing a responsive, single-page application (SPA) experience. The layout will dynamically adapt between desktop monitors and mobile browser screens. CSS media queries and responsive components will allow the desktop version to show full multi-column planning dashboards, while the mobile view offers a streamlined view focused on quick task entry and daily schedules.

Backend Framework (Python FastAPI or Node.js Express): The backend API handles calendar logic, recurring event generation, user authentication, and task management. It enforces Role-Based Access Control (RBAC) to manage feature visibility and permission constraints across different devices and user roles.

Database (PostgreSQL): A relational database will store structured user data, including user accounts, courses, recurring schedule patterns, task lists, and notes linked to specific appointments.

Containerization (Docker & Docker Compose): The entire application ecosystem—frontend UI, backend API, and database—will be packaged into isolated Docker containers. Using Docker ensures consistent runtime environments across development machines, simplifies local testing, and streamlines final deployment.
